===Etymology===
{{inh+|is|non|sjá}}, {{m|non|séa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*sehwaną}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to see, notice}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsjauː/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|auː|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|sá|sáu|séð}}

# to [[see]], to [[sense]] or [[perceive]] with one's [[eye]]s
#: {{ux|is|'''Sérðu''' illa?'' — ''Nei, ég '''sé''' mjög vel.|Have you got bad eyesight? — No, I '''see''' very well.}}
# to [[see]], to [[perceive]], to [[spot]]
#: {{syn|is|koma auga á}}
# to [[see]], to [[understand]]
#: {{syn|is|skilja|botna í}}
#: {{ux|is|Þú hlýtur að '''sjá''' hvað þetta er asnaleg hugmynd!|You must '''see''' what a stupid idea this is!}}

